To determine the range of a function, we need to identify the highest and lowest points on the y-axis. The highest point is 2 and the lowest point is 0.

The range of this function is the set of all possible y-values that the function can take. In this case, the range is the set of all real numbers between 0 and 2, inclusive.

*Answer*: {0, 2}
